  "note": "Election of the Kilkeel Urban Council, poll due Wednesday 18 May 1949; nominations received 4 May 1949 (Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1949, p. 3). Robert G. Hanna took the place of R. J. Ferguson, the outgoing Unionist member. The council was all Unionist. Returned unopposed."
